# Historical defect 1 and 3, reproduced: "latest" is `n.taken-day >
# r.taken-day`, so two same-day readings with different values both count as
# latest; and there is no upper bound on `taken-day`, so a reading dated after
# the decision can win.

rule fixture.latest-high v0.1
says "The holder's most recent alpha reading in the last 180 days is at least 70."

subject holder

collection readings : reading for subject via holder

conclude LatestHigh when
  some reading r in readings
  require r.test-code = alpha
  require r.amount >= 70
  require r.taken-day >= as-of-day - 180
  none of
    some reading n in readings
    require n.test-code = alpha
    require n.taken-day > r.taken-day
